Description:
Tchibo has set up projects to support farmers and their families in a number of coffee-growing countries. These projects all fall under the banner of Tchibo Joint Forces! The aim of the programme is to educate producers about more sustainable farming methods and to help them improve the quality of their coffee. Since 2017, our projects have increasingly included women and children, for example through activities and measures focusing on income support, childcare and preventing child labour.
 Farmer Trainings, Child Protection during harvest = Kindergardens, Awareness training on child labour, Climate Change adaptation through holistic approach, Diversification of farms, Demo Farms, Microfinancing, infrastructure, nursery;
 Business strengthening training;
 Farmer Trainings, demo plots establishment, next generation support, education of young people, - Last updated: December 2023.
